 people own at most 8% of the directory. It also lists Marco as active with 19% of lines, which is wrong against the truth (copy detection). Fails.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"B follows the rename and credits the lines to the original authors. Kochnev has 71% (within 68-82%). But it names Marco Silva as the only active author with 4 lines (4%), and it routes reviews to him, saying nobody active owns the code in delegators/. Marco has under 10% so it's acceptable. However it does state an active person with lines (Marco 4 lines) in the combined set, whereas the truth is 0%. This slightly violates 'an active person named as owner', but they are explicitly called a reviewer by default, not an owner. Passes narrowly.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"B credits Marco with 117 lines under one address in the exposure directory and says grouped_exposure.rb is 100% Marco's. This contradicts the truth (mostly Kochnev). It fails the criterion that the copied file not be credited to Marco.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"B says Lena's commit was set aside as boilerplate and dependabot's lines aren't counted. It says people with no commit in the last year own 89.3% (within 79-90%). But it does not say Subbota is active with about 3.3%, though it names Andrei Subbota as active. Peter Scholz is listed as inactive, with 7.9% (merge differs). The departed share and the Lena handling pass, and Scholz left and Subbota active are covered.\", \"pass\": true}], \"C\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"C says dblock has 119 commits and only about 242 surviving lines overall, which is roughly 4-5%, inside 3-8% if the repo has about 5,100 lines. Kochnev is named top by lines (1,190 including spec) and as having left in 2015. It does not give percentages explicitly, but the line counts imply them. Passes.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"C gives Kochnev 496 lines in exposure, which matches the truth (69%). It names McCarthy and Yunin as the next